# Student Package Manager

## Project Objective
This project is a beginner-friendly Java mini project that demonstrates the use of Java packages and import statements in a student management application. It is designed to help BCA students understand how to organize classes into different packages and reuse them across the project.

## Features
- Store student information: ID, name, course, and marks
- Create a `Student` class in the `model` package
- Create a `StudentManager` class in the `service` package
- Maintain a list of students using `ArrayList`
- Add students to the list
- Display all students
- Demonstrate Java packages clearly
- Demonstrate importing classes from one package into another
- Simple, clean, and suitable for a college-level tiny project
- No database and no external libraries used

## Package Structure
```text
studentmanager/
├── model/
│   └── Student.java
├── service/
│   └── StudentManager.java
└── app/
    └── Main.java
```

## Technologies Used
- Java
- Java Packages
- ArrayList collection
- Command-line compilation and execution

## How to Compile
Open the terminal in the project root and run:

```bash
javac studentmanager/model/Student.java studentmanager/service/StudentManager.java studentmanager/app/Main.java
```

## How to Run
After compiling, run:

```bash
java -cp . studentmanager.app.Main
```

